   "stem": {
      "text": "Consider the curve x^2 - y^2 + 6y = 18, for which dy/dx = x/(y - 3). How many points on the curve have a horizontal tangent line?"
   },
   "answer_key": {
      "form": "symbolic",
      "mathjson": 0
   },
   "worked_solution": [
      {
         "step": 1,
         "text": "A horizontal tangent needs the numerator to vanish, so x = 0.",
         "mathjson": 0
      },
      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "Substitute x = 0 into the curve: -y^2 + 6y = 18, so y^2 - 6y + 18 = 0, whose discriminant is 36 - 72 = -36.",
         "mathjson": [
            "Negate",
            36
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 3,
         "text": "The discriminant is negative, so no point of the curve has x = 0, and the curve has no point with a horizontal tangent. The count is 0.",
         "mathjson": 0
      }
   ],
